-- title:
--   Meet of incomparable invertible ideal sheaves with integral subschemes
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a scheme and let $I, J$ be quasi-coherent ideal sheaf data on $X$ (given by an ideal of $\Gamma(X,U)$ for each affine open $U$, compatible with restriction). Assume both are invertible in the sense of the project's predicate `IsInvertible`: for every point $x \in X$ there are an affine open $U \subseteq X$ and a section $f \in \Gamma(X,U)$ with $x$ in the basic open $X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\, f$, together with an element $g$ of $\Gamma(X, X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\, f)$ which is a non-zero-divisor, such that the ideal that $I$ (respectively $J$) assigns to the affine open $X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\, f$ is the principal ideal generated by $g$. Assume further that the closed subschemes $V(I)$ and $V(J)$ cut out by $I$ and $J$ are integral, i.e. nonempty, irreducible and reduced, and that $I$ and $J$ are incomparable: neither $I \le J$ nor $J \le I$ holds for the inclusion ordering of ideal sheaf data. Then the meet and the product of $I$ and $J$ coincide, $I \sqcap J = I \cdot J$.
--
--   This is the statement that two distinct prime effective Cartier divisors meet transversally at the level of ideal sheaves, $\mathcal O(-D_1) \cap \mathcal O(-D_2) = \mathcal O(-D_1-D_2)$; no Noetherian, regularity or factoriality hypothesis on $X$ is imposed. It is used in the analysis of the ideal sheaves of sections of the modular curve $X_1$, in [`ModularCurve.XOneP.isInvertible_ker_and_ker_mul_ker_eq_ker_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_twoChartModel_x1_mul`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOneP.isInvertible_ker_and_ker_mul_ker_eq_ker_of_map_maximalIdeal_eq_twoChartModel_x1_mul).
